      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "Real, fixed in d9accc88. The generation counter moved to where it belongs: `applyFolder` marks a write in flight (and bumps a write epoch before and after it), a refresh whose read overlapped a write is dropped, and while a write runs the overrides answer is held at what it was before it began, so recording the new hash first cannot switch this Mac's own overrides off for a moment. Test: a capture-start refresh in the middle of a write leaves `{ screenshotCopy: manual }` active (it fails without the hold)."
